1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,747
Day 51: minimind claims you can train a 64M parameter LLM from

2
00:00:05,747 --> 00:00:09,269
scratch in about two hours on one GPU.

3
00:00:09,269 --> 00:00:11,215
We tested that claim.

4
00:00:11,665 --> 00:00:16,259
minimind implements the full LLM training pipeline in pure

5
00:00:16,259 --> 00:00:19,190
PyTorch, with no high level wrappers.

6
00:00:19,190 --> 00:00:23,387
Its README says one RTX 3090 finishes pretraining and

7
00:00:23,387 --> 00:00:26,793
fine tuning in about two point three hours.

8
00:00:27,243 --> 00:00:30,581
We used the full official mini dataset and

9
00:00:30,581 --> 00:00:33,521
the stock defaults on an RTX 5060 Ti,

10
00:00:33,521 --> 00:00:36,461
changing only the epoch count to one.

11
00:00:36,911 --> 00:00:39,932
The SFT script loaded the pretrained checkpoint and

12
00:00:39,932 --> 00:00:42,716
trained on nine hundred thousand chat examples.

13
00:00:43,166 --> 00:00:46,556
Then we generated from both checkpoints with a fixed seed.

14
00:00:47,006 --> 00:00:49,333
Both stages finished with no errors,

15
00:00:49,333 --> 00:00:51,790
but took seven hours nineteen minutes,

16
00:00:51,790 --> 00:00:54,375
about three times the official estimate.

17
00:00:54,375 --> 00:00:57,284
The fine tuned model answered in chat format,

18
00:00:57,284 --> 00:00:58,965
yet still got facts wrong.

19
00:00:59,415 --> 00:01:03,935
Full logs and code are on GitHub, Apache-2.0 licensed.

20
00:01:03,935 --> 00:01:05,777
Write-up linked below.
